{"id": "EUVD-2026-71280", "enisaUuid": "57392a63-ccb8-3932-aae9-0f1a9a045c4e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: core: Add lock to usb_wakeup_notification()\n\nAdd a spin lock to usb_wakeup notification to prevent a race condition\nwith dereferencing freed memory. This could be hit by the xHCI driver as\nit calls this function from an IRQ and could race with the\nhub_disconnect() function, which properly grabs this lock to protect the\nstate of the device.", "datePublished": "2026-09-04T15:54:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:44:22", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a7a16167991c88016acef720927400404039d850", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/975ef630393c07fcbebf94f4d97043161b77a6ce", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/71cfda2fdf78041a01e9d94143baa79feabbdbf6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/04ab260407972e631c86f2bc576cd8e64d65b325", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bf2288583b4e072bdff17a233963619e4bc7a8b5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d80b946804674069db7ce6657319a71cf8eeaa5a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/960ca456faf61824b178f47967340300b24183db", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7c48aa0c1e79116b8af4b988d16ee29b427d6491", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e263e18a9e7b1ff3e7301f0801c6ff87c31adfb6"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-80830", "GHSA-6h45-3gcw-mpwf"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02cbf921-62b3-3571-9697-99672594d46b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.49"}, {"id": "1209298a-fd11-3143-867e-ac424a3e94cd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.108"}, {"id": "2146de79-5ffd-31f4-b86c-b9300df3fd8e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4ee823b83bc9851743fab756c76b27d6a1e2472b <975ef630393c07fcbebf94f4d97043161b77a6ce"}, {"id": "34109288-ce6a-39cc-87fc-f5e3b77ada2d", "product": {"name": "Linux",